{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"diagnosis\":\"The proof redundantly unpacks each bisimilarity witness into its underlying relation and bisimulation. Bisimilarity already exposes follow_fst and follow_snd, so transitions can be matched directly and the resulting bisimilarity inserted with ChoiceBisim.bisim.\",\"proof_body\":\"by\\n  intro hpq\\n  use @ChoiceBisim _ _ defs, ChoiceBisim.choice hpq\\n  intro s₁ s₂ hs μ\\n  constructor\\n  · intro s₁' ht\\n    cases hs with\\n    | choice hb =>\\n      cases ht with\\n      | choiceL ht =>\\n        obtain ⟨s₂', ht', hb'⟩ := hb.follow_fst ht\\n        exact ⟨s₂', Tr.choiceL ht', ChoiceBisim.bisim hb'⟩\\n      | choiceR ht =>\\n        refine ⟨s₁', Tr.choiceR ht, ChoiceBisim.bisim ?_⟩\\n        apply HomBisimilarity.refl\\n    | bisim hb =>\\n      obtain ⟨s₂', ht', hb'⟩ := hb.follow_fst ht\\n      exact ⟨s₂', ht', ChoiceBisim.bisim hb'⟩\\n  · intro s₂' ht\\n    cases hs with\\n    | choice hb =>\\n      cases ht with\\n      | choiceL ht =>\\n        obtain ⟨s₁', ht', hb'⟩ := hb.follow_snd ht\\n        exact ⟨s₁', Tr.choiceL ht', ChoiceBisim.bisim hb'⟩\\n      | choiceR ht =>\\n        refine ⟨s₂', Tr.choiceR ht, ChoiceBisim.bisim ?_⟩\\n        apply HomBisimilarity.refl\\n    | bisim hb =>\\n      obtain ⟨s₁', ht', hb'⟩ := hb.follow_snd ht\\n      exact ⟨s₁', ht', ChoiceBisim.bisim hb'⟩\"}"}}
